00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.410
Because justice!

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:56.540
Crazy.

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:58.500
I totally respect that.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.580
Stop it, brother bro.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:07.330
Now, Sherlock- <i>san</i> , it seems that Pu had
the motive you were so concerned about.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:14.370
Now all we need to do is find
the weapon he hid, and we're done.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.120
Calm down.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.450
Shut up!

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.040
It's not Pu! It can't be Pu!

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.830
He's not that stupid!

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.700
He wouldn't leave a clue like that!

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:28.660
He did seem smart.

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:31.750
He was going to be a doctor
or a lawyer, supposedly.

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:32.950
What do you mean?

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:35.200
His mom was saying that

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:38.910
he became a lawyer because
he was scared of seeing blood,

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:41.410
so he couldn't use a knife to kill him.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:45.250
The police didn't announce
what the weapon was yet.

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:46.410
Which means...

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:54.790
What's this?

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:56.620
Before he came to the Detective's Row House,

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.500
Pu went home and gave this to his mom.

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:01.500
Then it was him?

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:18.870
Now, I think it's time you
admitted your mistake.

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:21.950
When did I make a mistake?

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:23.120
We know that

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:27.250
Pu came here after the murder.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:27.250
Yes, of course!

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:30.200
The weapon's right there, baby.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:35.580
I'll call you again when we're done. Thanks.

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:38.790
It's great to have a friend, a buddy.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.910
Mr. Holmes.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:45.910
What's in that pocket?

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.870
It looked like a knife to me.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:51.000
The one used to kill Cosmos- <i>chan</i> .

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:53.080
Really?

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:55.370
The right pocket.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:01.410
This is the end, perhaps.

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:04.450
Now let's see it.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.660
Why'd this look like a knife to you?

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.330
Um...

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:30.040
When I stuck my hand in my pocket,
you weren't even in the room.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.750
How'd you know it was a knife?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:37.330
And the murder weapon, too?

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:41.120
What's going on here?

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.000
You wanna hear?

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.870
I sure do!

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:47.330
Please tell me!

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.120
Hey, old man.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:53.120
Give it up already!

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:56.370
Any idiot can tell that Pu did it!

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:58.660
There's plenty of evidence!

00:18:58.660 --> 00:19:00.040
That's the thing!

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:02.950
It doesn't make sense that
there's so much evidence!

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:06.500
Then if it's not Pu, who did it?

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:13.330
What caught my attention were the love
letters from Cosmos in Pu's mom's room.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:15.080
He just had a crush on her a long time ago!

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:18.370
But the mom chose Gaia, the younger brother.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.370
Pu's dad.

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:22.950
Well, sucks for him, I guess.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:27.000
But I want to know who killed Cosmos!

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:31.910
Cosmos is dead now.
Who cares what he was mad about?

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:35.700
What if Cosmos wasn't actually dead?

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:37.790
They found the body, right?

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:40.160
They only found a burnt corpse.

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.330
That's quibbling!

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:44.120
Cosmos and Pu were
the only ones in the room.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.160
And Pu's the only one who left!

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:49.790
So the body's gotta belong to Cosmos!

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:53.620
The body probably belongs to Pu's pops, Gaia.

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:58.620
Cosmos let Gaia stay with him in secret,

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.330
saying that he was helping him
hide from the loan sharks.

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:03.830
Then he called Pu over, got him drunk,

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:06.830
put his own clothes on Gaia's corpse,

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:10.120
put the knife in Pu's hands and started a fire.

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:14.450
Pu, panicked by the knife and the fire, fled.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:16.290
That's the deal.

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:21.000
So where the hell's Cosmos, then?

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.790
I just put the knife in my pocket.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:29.330
Only you, the person who was
with me, should know that.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.500
That's true.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:35.160
Then how'd B-zo know?

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:38.120
Cosmos told him.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:39.290
On the phone.

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:40.540
Shut up!

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:43.660
If Cosmos is the killer, then bring him here!

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.040
Stand by me! Now!

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:46.200
Now?

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:48.200
Yes! Just now!

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:50.500
As you like.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:06.580
You owed him a lot of money, too, right?

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:09.750
So you played your part in the farce.

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.750
The party's over.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:20.580
Oh, my god!

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:25.000
How is being a peeping tom different
from being arrested for murder?

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.700
I don't know, how?

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.580
One gives you a boner.
With the other, you're just boned.

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:30.540
A dirty joke, huh?

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:32.950
That's all the time we have for today.

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:37.950
So, let's talk about our future.

00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:38.910
Our future?

00:21:38.910 --> 00:21:42.290
I don't mind an age difference, after all.

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:43.790
Age difference?

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:46.750
" <i>Western Dream</i>
B-zo Uchida"

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.950
B-zo... Goodbye.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.080
Get cleaning!

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:59.000
You're behind schedule! Get to it!

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:01.910
Your share of the space is this one sofa.

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:03.620
Don't stick out from it by a millimeter!

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:04.790
Okay.

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:06.540
So about my job...

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:09.450
Someone was watching me the
whole time from behind my mirror--

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:10.950
Never mind! Leave!

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:05.040
"The Water's Usually Hot"

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:05.040
Your front door's unlocked-German-suplex!

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:07.080
"What Do We Know About Jack the Ripper?"
"See you next week!"
